      "description": "In $|x - 3| < |x + 1|$ both sides are non-negative, and for non-negative numbers $P < Q \\iff P^2 < Q^2$.",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p2",
      "description": "In $|x - 1| < x - 5$ the right-hand side is negative for $x < 5$; squaring would then give wrong solutions (in fact the inequality has no solution).",
      "marks": 1
     }
    ]
   },
   "markingNotes": "Example answer: Squaring preserves an inequality only between non-negative numbers. Both moduli are non-negative, so squaring the first is safe. In the second, $x - 5$ can be negative, and then the inequality is false whatever $x$ is, but squaring could suggest solutions. Using critical values shows $|x - 1| < x - 5$ has no solution at all."
  },
